<!--Workspace Documentation — ArchitectureOverview
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.renderer.workspace.documentation.ArchitectureOverview-->
<wsdocumentation:ArchitectureOverview xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:wsdocumentation="com.machineblocks.bml.renderer.workspace.documentation"
  xmlns:engine="org.blockml.bml.engine.blockrender"
  xmlns:render="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render"
  xmlns:mbcli="com.machineblocks.bml.cli">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    How the engine, render target, and host CLI compose
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Three packages, one product path: BML in, MachineBlocks V3 SCAD out.

    @blockml/block-render-engine implements the RenderEngine contract (the
    CompilerEngine). It does not know MachineBlocks. Processors call
    compile, renderTemplate, renderTemplates, copyTemplate, or callLLM.
    One target may mix those strategies. callLLM is specified and deferred.

    @machineblocks/render-target is a RenderTarget named machineblocks-v3-scad.
    It depends on the engine and on @machineblocks/core. V1 processors cover
    com.machineblocks.bml.core.Block and com.machineblocks.bml.core.Set.
    Mappings are declarative. The target is browser and Node compatible: no
    Node-only APIs.

    @machineblocks/cli depends on @blockml/cli and on the render target. It
    registers machineblocks-v3-scad, applies MachineBlocks defaults (library
    path, OpenSCAD path, output), and is the command MachineBlocks users run.
    @blockml/cli stays domain-agnostic and does not register this target.

    A content project holds BML sources and generated SCAD. It installs
    @machineblocks/cli (and through it the target, the engine, and
    @machineblocks/core). It does not need the blockml source repository.

    Delegate-only targets (for example a domain that only adds Block types)
    may list this render target as a delegate and ship no engine of their own.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="wsdocumentation:ReadingOrder" relation="ReadNext" />
    <see type="engine:README" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="render:README" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="mbcli:README" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</wsdocumentation:ArchitectureOverview>
